==Enemy==
Super Metal Hippoe is a larger, stronger and faster version of [[Metal Hippoe]]. With his guaranteed [[Knockback|knockback]] ability, quick movement speed, and high health, he can be a very annoying enemy to fight.

This Metal enemy, unlike [[Sir Metal Seal]], tends to appear in stages that otherwise have little to no Metal enemies, such as [[Saucy Scandals]] or [[Oil Spill Rainbow]]. Super Metal Hippoe also tends to appear in groups of two or three in some stages, such as [[Total Myopia]] and [[March to Death (Merciless)|March to Death]].

==Strategy==
It is important to note that like all other Metal enemies, Super Metal Hippoe takes only one damage from any attack, unless it is a [[Critical Hit]]. Combined with his very high health, [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] are basically mandatory to properly fight him.

[[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Cat]] is a great choice for beginners as he outranges Super Metal Hippoe, allowing him to be stacked to increase the chance of a Critical Hit. [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]] can also be used with care to deal heavy damage; at higher levels and in [[True Form]], she can even one-shot Super Metal Hippoe. Likewise, nearly any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] or [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]] with Critical Hits has potential to be extremely effective against him, with [[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Berserker Cat]], [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]] and [[Kyosaka Nanaho (Legend Rare Cat)|Kyosaka Nanaho]] being some of the most reliable options overall.
	
Since Super Metal Hippoe pushes hard with his knockback ability, Meatshields lacking knockback immunity such as [[Primordial Cat (Rare Cat)|Modern Cat]] are not as effective. [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] can absorb several hits and prevent Super Metal Hippoe from pushing thanks to his knockback immunity, but he needs HP [[Talents]] in order for him to consistently tank hits at higher magnifications.

